{
  "uid": "supply-chain",
  "title": "Supply chain — what is running, and what is known about it",
  "tags": [
    "security",
    "supply-chain",
    "cve",
    "mdapi"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "links": [],
  "refresh": "5m",
  "schemaVersion": 36,
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "version": 1,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {
          "text": "Prometheus",
          "value": "Prometheus"
        },
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Two layers, and neither is sufficient alone.** Build-time scanning covers what you make; runtime scanning covers what you *pull* — third-party images never went through your pipeline. These figures are the runtime layer: every image actually running, rescanned four times a day in rotating batches.\n\n⭐ **Read the *fixable* count, not the total.** A critical CVE with no upstream fix is a risk to accept and document; a critical CVE with a fix available is a rebuild you have not done. Only the second is actionable, and only the second belongs on a dashboard.\n\n⚠️ Measured 2026-09-22: Grype and Trivy agree on only **81%** of findings for the same Debian image, and on an Alpine image one reported 7 vulnerabilities where the other reported *Clean*. A single scanner is not coverage.\n\n*Scope: only **critical** and **high** are tracked. Medium and low on 146 running images is a number nobody acts on, and a dashboard nobody acts on trains people to ignore the ones that matter. Source: `f/probe/pod_image_cve_scan`.*"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Images scanned",
      "description": "Distinct images actually running and rescanned on rotation.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "pod_image_cve_scan_images_total",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Critical, fix available",
      "description": "The actionable number: a fix exists upstream and has not been pulled in.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(pod_image_cve_count{severity=\"critical\",fix_state=\"fixed\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 20
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "High, fix available",
      "description": "Same reading as critical, one severity down.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(pod_image_cve_count{severity=\"high\",fix_state=\"fixed\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 50
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Components with an upgrade waiting",
      "description": "Platform components behind their latest release. Distinct from CVEs: this is cadence, not exposure.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(component_upgrade_available)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Fixable vulnerabilities over time — rebuild cadence made visible",
      "description": "A sawtooth on the fixable lines is healthy: it means rebuilds land. A rising flat line means the daily patch layer has stopped reaching the registry. The third line is a different conversation entirely — nothing to rebuild, so it belongs in the risk register, not in a backlog.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(pod_image_cve_count{severity=\"critical\",fix_state=\"fixed\"})",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "critical, fixable"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(pod_image_cve_count{severity=\"high\",fix_state=\"fixed\"})",
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "high, fixable"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(pod_image_cve_count{severity=\"critical\",fix_state=\"unfixed\"})",
          "refId": "C",
          "legendFormat": "critical, NO fix available"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Images carrying fixable critical or high findings",
      "description": "Ranked by what can actually be fixed today. Rebuild from the top; an image with only unfixable findings belongs in the risk register, not here.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "$datasource"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(20, sum by (image) (pod_image_cve_count{severity=~\"critical|high\",fix_state=\"fixed\"}))",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "job": true,
              "prometheus": true,
              "service": true,
              "instance": true,
              "namespace": true,
              "endpoint": true,
              "container": true,
              "pod": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "image": "Image",
              "Value": "Fixable critical + high"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Fixable critical + high",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    }
  ]
}
